{% comment %}
  Step 3 (shown as "Step 2 of 5" once wired) — pick a day and time slot.

  Day strip, calendar modal, and time-slot grid are all JS-driven — see the
  "SLOT PICKER" section of kal-booking-flow.js. Mirrors the real staff CMS's
  SlotPicker.tsx mechanics exactly:
  - Day strip: today + next 9 days (matches STRIP_DAYS = 10 in SlotPicker.tsx),
    generated client-side, no API call needed.
  - Calendar modal: month grid, chevron nav clamped to [today, today+90 days]
    (MAX_FUTURE_DAYS), past/beyond-cap cells disabled.
  - Time slots: GET /api/public/availability/slots?doctor_id=&date=&facility_id=&duration_minutes=45,
    grouped into Morning/Afternoon/Evening client-side (6-12 / 12-16 / 16-22,
    same ranges as SlotPicker.tsx). Slots come back for the whole day and are
    rendered disabled+struck-through when is_available is false, rather than
    omitted — same as the real CMS (SlotPicker.tsx line ~386).
  - Mode filtering matches SlotPicker.tsx exactly: video/online mode filters
    client-side to slot_type "online"/"both" (no facility_id sent); in-clinic
    mode sends facility_id and relies on the RPC's own facility join to scope
    results, no client-side slot_type filter needed.

  Doctor id/facility id are still placeholders (data-kal-doctor-id/
  data-kal-facility-id on the wrapper below) — real values come from whichever
  doctor was picked in the previous step, once doctor-selection data fetching
  is wired (explicitly deferred, see build log). Doctor summary card text is
  still dummy for the same reason.

  Left column reuses .kal-step-entry__info (desktop), same as the other steps.

  The calendar modal itself lives in kal-booking-flow.liquid, not here — see
  the comment there for why (overflow-clipping bug when nested inside the
  scrollable content area).
{% endcomment %}

{%- comment -%}
  data-kal-doctor-id / data-kal-facility-id: PLACEHOLDER values (a real
  doctor/facility pair from the CMS — Neethu Jayachandran at Kerala Ayurveda,
  Koramangala — used so slot fetching hits real availability data). Once
  doctor-selection is wired to real backend data, the doctor-card click
  handler should just overwrite these two attributes before navigating here —
  the slot-picker JS itself reads them fresh on every fetch and needs no
  other change.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="kal-step-slot-picker" data-kal-doctor-id="0f425bd1-9a69-4adc-a0a3-6f2b8ba87191" data-kal-facility-id="185b85d7-fad2-405d-b8ea-13dc683fbde8">

  {%- comment -%} ============ MOBILE ONLY (below 750px) ============ {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="kal-step-slot-picker__mobile">

    <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__header">
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__back" data-kal-back="doctor-select" aria-label="Back">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'chevron-left' -%}
      </button>
      <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress">
        <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot"></span>
        <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot--active"></span>
        <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot"></span>
        <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot"></span>
        <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot"></span>
        <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-text">2/5</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Reuses the same eyebrow/heading classes as the Doctor Select step's
      intro block (kal-step-doctor-select__eyebrow/__heading) — those classes
      aren't actually scoped to that one step, same convention as
      .kal-step-entry__info being reused on the desktop composition.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__intro">
      <p class="kal-step-doctor-select__eyebrow">Step 2 of 5</p>
      <h2 class="kal-step-doctor-select__heading">Pick your visit</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-doctor-summary" data-kal-doctor-summary>
      <span class="kal-doctor-summary__avatar"></span>
      <span class="kal-doctor-summary__info">
        <span class="kal-doctor-summary__name" data-kal-summary-name>Dr. Meera Pillai</span>
        <span class="kal-doctor-summary__meta" data-kal-summary-meta>General Physician - 12yrs</span>
      </span>
      <span class="kal-doctor-summary__mode" data-kal-summary-mode>Online</span>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-slot-section">
      <div class="kal-slot-section__head">
        <p class="kal-slot-section__label">Choose a day</p>
        <button type="button" class="kal-icon-button" data-kal-open-calendar aria-label="Open calendar">
          {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'calendar-days' -%}
        </button>
      </div>
      {%- comment -%} Populated client-side by renderDayStrip() in kal-booking-flow.js {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="kal-day-strip" data-kal-day-strip></div>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-slot-section">
      <p class="kal-slot-section__label">Available time</p>
      {%- comment -%} Populated client-side by renderSlotPeriods() in kal-booking-flow.js {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="kal-slot-periods" data-kal-slot-periods>
        <p class="kal-slot-periods__empty">Loading available times&hellip;</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-slot-picker__footer">
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue" data-kal-goto="patient-details" data-kal-slot-continue disabled>
        Select a date and time
      </button>
    </div>

  </div>

  {%- comment -%} ============ DESKTOP (750px and up) — matches Figma Frame 4 exactly ============ {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="kal-step-slot-picker__desktop">
    <div class="kal-step-entry__info">
      <div class="kal-step-entry__info-content">
        <h2 class="kal-step-entry__heading">Pick your visit</h2>
        <p class="kal-step-entry__body-text">
          Book a consultation in under a minute in-clinic or video. Confirmation
          arrives instantly, no account required.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="kal-step-entry__location">
        <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--location">
          <!-- ICON: location-pin (not received yet) -->
        </span>
        <span class="kal-step-entry__location-text">
          Kerala Ayurveda Wellness Center, Kormangala &middot; Opens 8 AM
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-slot-picker__panel">
      <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress kal-step-doctor-select__progress--desktop">
        <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot"></span>
        <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot--active"></span>
        <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot"></span>
        <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot"></span>
        <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot"></span>
        <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-text">2/5</span>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-step-slot-picker__scroll">
        <div class="kal-doctor-summary" data-kal-doctor-summary>
          <span class="kal-doctor-summary__avatar"></span>
          <span class="kal-doctor-summary__info">
            <span class="kal-doctor-summary__name" data-kal-summary-name>Dr. Neethu</span>
            <span class="kal-doctor-summary__meta" data-kal-summary-meta>General Physician - 12yrs</span>
          </span>
          <span class="kal-doctor-summary__mode" data-kal-summary-mode>Online</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kal-slot-section">
          <div class="kal-slot-section__head">
            <p class="kal-slot-section__label">Choose a day</p>
            <button type="button" class="kal-icon-button" data-kal-open-calendar aria-label="Open calendar">
              {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'calendar-days' -%}
            </button>
          </div>
          {%- comment -%} Populated client-side by renderDayStrip() in kal-booking-flow.js {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="kal-day-strip" data-kal-day-strip></div>
        </div>

        <div class="kal-slot-section">
          <p class="kal-slot-section__label">Available time</p>
          {%- comment -%} Populated client-side by renderSlotPeriods() in kal-booking-flow.js {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="kal-slot-periods" data-kal-slot-periods>
            <p class="kal-slot-periods__empty">Loading available times&hellip;</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__desktop-footer">
        <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue" data-kal-goto="patient-details" data-kal-slot-continue disabled>
          Select a date and time
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>
